  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Humanitarian Prioritisation and Operational Analysis in Palestine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen evidence-based humanitarian prioritisation and response planning across Palestine, including in Gaza and the West Bank. The project will generate robust, multi-sector evidence on household vulnerability, food security, shelter conditions, service access, displacement dynamics, and market functionality to support humanitarian prioritisation and targeting. Through large-scale household assessments, vulnerability profiling, qualitative research, shelter and service analysis, and market assessments, the project will provide humanitarian actors with the data and analysis needed to design more effective, evidence-based responses in a highly constrained and evolving humanitarian context.</narrative>
  </description>
